{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQtZBEVQwx5T6SbZpid","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack` so it only refuses once body bytes have been written. Before, it also refused right after the headers were sent, which broke WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket`: they send the headers first and then hijack the connection.\n\n- **`response_writer.go`:** the guard is now `if w.size > 0` instead of `if w.Written()`. Hijacking works before any write and after `WriteHeaderNow()`, but still fails with `errHijackAlreadyWritten` once body data has gone out.\n- **`response_writer_test.go`:** I added a test case showing that hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` succeeds.\n\n`go test ./...` passes.\n\nI haven't tested this against a real WebSocket library, only with the mock hijacker. Nothing is committed yet; say if you want it committed under that message."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":799,"cache_read_input_tokens":34724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":799,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bae89ae1-19ab-424d-8282-48a1becc8483","uuid":"c750d249-7724-445a-96df-4e0c18d55ff8","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:28:34.370Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQtYyLhR2xtufUT8QRQ"}
